    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2024/12/saucony-ride-18-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The reworked PWRRUN+ provides moderate cushioning and impact protection with a slightly firm ride, and the heel feels a bit softer than the forefoot.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is moderate with a touch of TPU bounce, but it is less aggressively bouncy/snappy than the prior version and not a true speed-focused feel.",
        "Stability: Heel hold is improved by added collar padding plus a stiff heel counter, midfoot lockdown is secure, and overall torsional behavior is moderate due to mild-to-moderate flexibility.",
        "Durability: Durability is a key strength with resilient materials and added outsole coverage; despite some slightly earlier outsole wear than the predecessor, expected lifespan is still average to above average."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2024/12/saucony-ride-18-multi-tester-review.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: PWRRUN+ midsole and cushioned insole deliver a soft, forgiving underfoot feel with ample impact protection at a moderate 35/27 mm stack; the heel can feel lower/softer at slower paces, while the forefoot feels flexible and agile.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is lively with decent energy return and moderate bounce, but not standout; toe-off is slightly more responsive than Ride 17 yet still less snappy/decisive than older Ride versions.",
        "Stability: Stable-neutral (slightly stability-leaning) with excellent midfoot lockdown and a rigid, extended heel counter for strong heel hold; lateral support is secure from the structured upper, while torsional feel remains moderate because the shoe is quite flexible and unplated.",
        "Durability: Outsole rubber coverage and lug patterning are broad with good wet-surface grip, and testers expect strong longevity with wear resistance consistent with Ride models that often last hundreds of miles."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/saucony-ride-18-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Ride 18 uses dual-density PWRRUN Plus (softer insole over firmer midsole) for soft step-in comfort, solid impact protection, and a forgiving heel/forefoot feel without becoming mushy.",
        "Responsiveness: The TPU-beaded PWRRUN Plus delivers clear energy return and pop, with testers noting easy pace pick-ups and a snappy-enough ride for faster efforts.",
        "Stability: The shoe is described as a stable, reasonably firm platform with secure lockdown from the gusseted tongue, loop lacing, and padded heel area; no explicit torsional-rigidity or heel-counter test data is provided.",
        "Durability: The TPU-beaded foam is called out for strong longevity, and the XT-900 outsole supports durability expectations, though wet-surface performance is a weakness and long-term outsole wear data is not reported."
      ]
    }
